# Real ballot-level preference data for the 2022 Orkney Islands Council election, Ward 1 -
# Kirkwall East (5 candidates, 4 seats). Converted from
# https://github.com/mggg/scot-elex/blob/main/5_cands/orkney_2022_ward1.csv (MGGG's public
# archive of real Scottish STV preference profiles, described in arXiv:2605.12676).
# Cross-checked against Orkney Islands Council's official Declaration of Results PDF
# (declaration-of-results-ward-1-kirkwall-east.pdf, orkney.gov.uk): 1694 valid votes, quota
# 339, first preferences Dawson 285 / Heddle 428 / Macdonald 92 / Scott 476 / Shearer 413;
# Heddle, Scott, and Shearer elected at stage 1, Dawson at stage 2, Macdonald not elected.
# Round 2/4 intermediate tallies additionally cross-checked against Orkney's official
# "Candidate Votes Per Stage Report" for this ward (candidate-votes-per-stage-ward-1-kirkwall-
# east.pdf): Heddle, Scott, and Shearer all meet quota simultaneously in stage 1; stage 2
# transfers Scott's surplus (137, the largest), giving Dawson 340.54733 and Macdonald
# 134.02026 -- see ScottishRealElectionFixtureTest for the round-by-round spot-checks.
